# Feature traceability: every row of docs/FEATURES.md -> the automated tests that prove it.
#
# Checked by scripts/traceability.sh (make traceability, and CI). It fails when
#   * a FEATURES.md row has no entry here, or an entry has no reference;
#   * an entry here names a row that no longer exists;
#   * a referenced test no longer exists.
#
# Format. A header line "[<section>] <feature>" (the "## " heading and the first
# table cell of the row), then indented reference lines:
#   unit <module> <test>      fn <test> in oxpanel-daemon/src/<module>.rs (mod tests)
#   it <file> <test>          fn <test> in oxpanel-daemon/tests/<file>.rs
#   sh <path> <text>          the text occurs in a check of that shell suite
#                             (tests-integration/run-inside.sh, tests-acceptance/phases/NN-*.sh)
# Integration checks run in a systemd container (make integration) and again on
# the real SELinux host (make acceptance, phase 20); phases 30-90 only there.

